OVERVIEW: Open the dashboard in your browser, optionally at an area.

Areas: home, flags, apps, claims, devices, analytics, vrt, releases, feedback,
support, webhooks, alerts, keys, team, audit, settings, billing. With --json
the URL is printed instead of opened.

USAGE: grantiva console open [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [<area>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <area>                  Dashboard area. Default: the dashboard home. (values:
                          home, flags, apps, claims, devices, analytics, vrt,
                          releases, feedback, support, webhooks, alerts, keys,
                          team, audit, settings, billing; default: home)

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

